# E23c -- Get a REAL invasion onto the map and find out whether v5.8's exclusion holds against one. Addendum 49 ships the rule that DF's own invaders (invasion_id >= 0) leave every layer count, because one raid can make a cavern look stocked and silence the job that keeps it alive — and that rule has still never met an invader. E23b pinned all three cavern features at the documented maximum of 100,000 for two full seasons with no decay whatever and drew ZERO invaders, 2 of 2, so irritation is not sufficient; CTRL's own cavern irritation sits at 0 and never rises, which is what a fort that has never breached a cavern looks like. This takes the other road: 53.16's timed_event_type carries EvaluateAttackAndSendImmediateArmy, which DFHack's `force` accepts (it refuses only FeatureAttack, and only because it passes feature_ind = -1). An army invasion carries invasion_id just as a cavern raid does, so it exercises the same exclusion without needing an open cavern. A season on CTRL, two replicates each, with the tool's land and cavern layers managed so the counts under test are the shipped ones.
run 20260918-215125 fort CTRL backup CTRL.preverify
DF v0.53.16 win64 STEAM DFHack 53.16-r1.1 world The Legendary Dimension site 32 tiles 29..29,20..20 seed WILDERPOP1
commits: DwarfCron 835fddb seasonal-wildlife 41bbd19 fps cap 1000

## Predictions (written before the run)
- the exclusion works: invaders appear, invaders>0 is logged with their species, and the land and cavern counts never move with them
- the exclusion is a silent no-op: invaders appear and the layer counts rise with them, which means WILD.field resolved wrongly on this build — though E23b already showed it resolving to invasion_id, so this is now unlikely
- the event is accepted and nothing comes: force returns ok, the event is queued and then consumed, and no unit ever carries invasion_id >= 0 — the army needs a hostile civ with a route, which a quiet year-2 fort may not have
- force refuses it: the command errors, and an invasion cannot be raised from the event queue on 53.16 at all; the exclusion then stays untestable until a fort digs into a cavern

